    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31-a1">

                <pb facs="0148" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg52"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The imperial royal minister for
                            foreign affairs to Mr. Jay.</hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Appendix</hi>
                </p>
                <p>As a preliminary response due to the esteemed note of the 17th instant, the
                    contents of which the undersigned minister of the imperial house and for foreign
                    affairs communicated without delay to the imperial royal minister of commerce,
                    the undersigned is glad to be enabled to inform Mr. John Jay, envoy
                    extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of the United States of America, that
                    the undersigned has already been advised by that minister that he will soon be
                    ready to present to the Reichsrath the project of a special law for the
                    provisional protection of articles introduced at the Vienna Exposition.</p>
                <p>The undersigned, &amp;c., for the minister for foreign affairs.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ORCZY.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-03-25"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 25,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
